## 3.3 Lifecycle Information

### Purpose

The Lifecycle Information section records the current engineering lifecycle status of a System Objective and its progression through the approved governance process.

Its purpose is to provide visibility into the objective's maturity, approval status, and engineering readiness.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following lifecycle fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Current Lifecycle Stage | Current approved lifecycle stage of the objective. |
| Lifecycle Status Date | Date the current stage became effective. |
| Previous Lifecycle Stage | Immediately preceding lifecycle stage, where applicable. |
| Transition Reason | Engineering justification for the latest lifecycle transition. |
| Approval Reference | Reference to the approval authorizing the transition. |

---

### Lifecycle Rules

Lifecycle information shall:

- Reflect the current approved status of the objective.
- Be updated only through approved governance processes.
- Preserve historical lifecycle transitions.
- Remain consistent with the Objective Governance framework.

---

### Engineering Note

Lifecycle information records the governance state of an objective.

It does not describe changes to the engineering content, which are managed through versioning and change history.
